==Commonly used magic shops==
*For [[elemental rune|elemental]], [[chaos rune|chaos]] and [[death rune]]s: [[Betty's Magic Emporium]] in [[Port Sarim]], [[Aubury's Rune Shop]] in [[Varrock]], and [[Void Knight Magic Store]] in [[Void Knights' Outpost]].
*[[Lundail's Arena-side Rune Shop]] in the [[Mage Arena]], accessible without any requirements, is one of the few rune shops that also sells [[Law rune|law]], [[Nature rune|nature]] and [[cosmic rune]]s. However, it is risky for hardcore and ultimate ironmen due to travelling through the [[Wilderness]].
*[[Ali Morrisane]] in [[Al Kharid]] also sells [[Law rune|law]], [[Nature rune|nature]] and [[cosmic rune]]s, though at a lower stock and a higher price than [[Lundail]]. However, it is safe for hardcore and ultimate ironmen. Unlocking the rune shop requires completion of [[The Feud]] quest and doing the runes section of [[Rogue Trader]]. The shop also buys runes at a set price, unlike in other shops.
*[[Wizards' Guild]] in [[Yanille]] sells all runes except [[cosmic rune]]s, [[astral rune]]s, [[combination rune]]s, and [[wrath rune]]s. Level 66 Magic and completion of [[The Hand in the Sand]] is required to access it.
*[[Baba Yaga's Magic Shop]] on [[Lunar Isle]] is the only shop that sells [[astral rune]]s. Accessible after the [[Lunar Diplomacy]] quest.
*[[Amlodd's Magical Supplies]] in [[Prifddinas]] sells [[cosmic rune]]s in large quantities. Completion of the [[Song of the Elves]] quest is required to access this shop. 
*[[Tal Teklan Rune Shop]] in [[Tal Teklan]] sells [[Nature rune|nature]] and [[Cosmic rune|cosmic runes]] in small quantities. It is notable for its easy accessibility early, access to [[Varlamore]] being the only requirement. 

== Obtaining Magic Equipment ==
The [[Rune pouch]] can be obtained very early on in an Ironman's progression through [[Last Man Standing]] and [[Mage Training Arena]] or later through [[Slayer]], and is incredibly helpful for saving inventory space across all of the games' activities.

=== Weapons ===

* Each type of [[Elemental staves|elemental staff]] can be bought at [[Zaff's Superior Staffs!]] with a bit of starting cash.
** [[Wind spells|Wind spells']] scaling damage can be cast with only [[Catalytic rune|catalytic runes]], making them a cost effective way to use Magic at a low level.
* [[Iban's staff]] is awarded upon completion of [[Underground Pass]] and can be used to cast [[Iban Blast]] at level 50 Attack and Magic. This is the strongest early Magic weapon for non-elemental weakness targets, possessing a max hit of 25. It is strongly recommended to pay {{Coins|200000}} to the [[Dark Mage]] to upgrade the charge capacity on the staff from 120 to 2,500.
* The [[Ancient staff]] can be acquired for {{Coins|80000}} from [[Eblis]] after [[Desert Treasure I]]. It is helpful for auto-casting spells on the [[Ancient Magicks]] spellbook.
* The [[Warped sceptre]] can be obtained from [[Slayer task/Warped creature|Warped creatures]] after [[The Path of Glouphrie]] with 56 [[Slayer]]
* [[Ahrim's staff]], [[Blue moon spear]], and the [[Ancient sceptre]] all provide 5% magic damage and can be acquired from [[Barrows]], [[Moons of Peril]], and [[Phantom Muspah]] respectively. The sceptre gives additional benefits and autocast to Ancient Magicks as well.
* The [[Twinflame staff]] can be crafted from drops from the [[Royal Titans]] and provides the best damage output on the [[standard spellbook]] before access to [[Wrath rune|wrath runes]].
* The [[Trident of the seas]] can be acquired from [[cave kraken]] with 87 Slayer on a kraken task.
** This can be further upgraded with a [[Magic fang]] from [[Zulrah]] into a [[Trident of the swamp]]
* Endgame magic weapons include the [[Staff of the dead]], (and its [[Toxic staff of the dead|upgraded Toxic variant]]), from [[K'ril Tsutsaroth]], the [[Eye of ayak|Eye of Ayak]] from [[Doom of Mokhaiotl]], the [[Sanguinesti staff]] from [[Theatre of Blood]], [[Tumeken's shadow]] from [[Tombs of Amascut]], and the [[nightmare staff]] and its variants from [[The Nightmare]].

=== Armour ===

* Magic accuracy from equipment is not very impactful early on, as most monsters you use magic on have little to no magic defence. However, the [[wizard hat]], [[Blue wizard robe|wizard robe top]], and [[Zamorak monk bottom]] can provide some magic accuracy in a pinch.
* [[Mystic robes]] can be received as a drop from [[Slayer monsters]] or purchased from the [[Wizards' Guild]] after 66 Magic.
* The [[Tome of fire]] and [[Tome of water]] can be obtained as rare drops from their respective skilling bosses, [[Wintertodt]] and [[Tempoross]]. They provide a small buff to their respective elemental spells, but are primarily beneficial as a source of infinite Fire and Water runes in the offhand for non-combat spells. 
** The [[Tome of earth]] can be obtained much later as a rare drop from [[The Hueycoatl]].
* [[Mage Arena I]] and [[Mage Arena II|II]] can be completed at 60 and 75 Magic, respectively, and award powerful magic capes. The best-in-slot [[Imbued magic cape|Imbued god capes]] provide some of the earliest sources of Magic damage.
* [[Void Knight equipment]] and especially [[Elite Void Knight equipment]] after the [[Hard Western Provinces Diary]] provide powerful magic accuracy and damage boosts.
* [[Ahrim the Blighted's equipment|Ahrim's]], [[Blue moon armour|Blue moon]], [[Bloodbark armour|Bloodbark]], [[Infinity robes|Infinity]], and [[Dagon'hai robes]] all provide similar magic accuracy and damage but can be obtained in vastly different ways. Ahrim's and Blue moon equipment are often acquired alongside other armour sets, but Bloodbark and Infinity can be acquired through their own mini-games offering different rewards.
* [[Mage's book]] can be acquired from the [[Mage Training Arena]], while the [[Elidinis' ward]] can be acquired as a drop in [[Tombs of Amascut]].
* The [[Tormented bracelet]] can be made with a [[Zenyte shard]] from [[Demonic gorilla|Demonic gorillas]] with 95 [[Crafting]].
* The [[Occult necklace]] can be obtained from [[Smoke devil|Smoke devils]] or the [[Thermonuclear smoke devil]] at 93 Slayer
* Endgame magic armour includes [[Eternal boots]] from [[Cerberus]], [[Virtus robes]] from the [[The Forgotten Four]], [[Ancestral robes]] from [[Chambers of Xeric]], [[Magus ring]] from [[Duke Sucellus]], [[Imbued heart]] and [[Saturated heart]] from [[Superior slayer monster|superior slayer monsters]], and the [[Arcane sigil]] to upgrade Elidinis' ward from [[Corporeal Beast]].
